ills mostly not granted, and would double-read on Juggling); it is ability text. || RELATED: four at level one, two more at levels 4, 7, 11 and 15. Communications +5, Domestic, Espionage +5, Horsemanship General and Exotic Animals only, Physical except Boxing, Pilot except robot and military vehicles (the Robot Combat, Robots & Power Armor and Military: rows), Rogue +10, Technical, W.P. except Heavy Weapons (both heavy W.P. rows) and Pole Arm. || SECONDARY: two at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12, none at level one: count 0 with a schedule. || HAND TO HAND: none granted; one may be chosen, never better than Basic, so hand_to_hand costs basic 1 and nothing else. || EQUIPMENT: stored by catalog slug: clothing x2 (a couple sets), Vibro-Knife, small-silver-cross, pocket-mirror, backpack, duffle bag, 1D4 sacks, sleeping-bag for the bedroll, canteen, portable language translator, sunglasses, and weapons-matching-w-p-skills for one weapon per W.P. No catalog row for costumes, jacket, juggling pins, the wooden and silver-plated throwing knives (they carry their own damage; knife-throwing is not the same item), makeup kit, wine skin or pocket calculator; the E-Clips are per W.P. and left in prose. They are a restriction line. || MONEY: 2D6x100 credits stored; 1D4x1,000 in trade goods is not coin. || NOT STORED: size, weight, life span, breeding, habitat, allies and enemies are in GM Notes."
